      "writtenOn": "2024-11-18T16:02:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not entirely sold on this. What does the current usage look like, can you reference the internal API usages that this is currently hitting?\n\nBut otherwise an API that might take effect somewhere between \"immediately\" and \"never\" seems sketchy. A consumer is required to support the previous/initial usage bits indefinitely after creation after all. So why do the usage bits need to change at all?",
      "revId": "af80ce31dfa861b7b912518aeb7523583af84e31",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "16a3d299_da71db47",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1156740
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-18T17:48:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this is usage for Encoder, our persistent input surface can be utilized by multiple encoder instances(not simultaneously) one by one. Each encoder could have different consumer usage. (e.g. s/w encoder and h/w encoder)\n\nAnd of course, there will be cleaning-up and set-up regarding disconnecting from the previous encoder and connecting the current encoder.\n\nconsumer usage is retrieved from the encoder instance around here, and set to `config-\u003emIsConfig-\u003emUsage` in just a little bit below.\n\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/av/media/codec2/sfplugin/CCodec.cpp;drc\u003d454ac2b3e6024e004f7665dc07b6c3d23d1fd4fb;l\u003d1597\n\nAnd the retrieved usage is set here.\n\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/av/media/module/bqhelper/GraphicBufferSource.cpp;drc\u003d454ac2b3e6024e004f7665dc07b6c3d23d1fd4fb;l\u003d1194\n\n(called from here https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/av/media/codec2/sfplugin/CCodec.cpp;drc\u003d454ac2b3e6024e004f7665dc07b6c3d23d1fd4fb;l\u003d507 )",
      "parentUuid": "6bfe1400_b29a07f4",
      "revId": "af80ce31dfa861b7b912518aeb7523583af84e31",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ee8cee7e_f1668bc4",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010103
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-18T18:48:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "if this:\n\n```\n * \u003cp\u003eNote: If the AImageReader is already connected to an output,\n * the new usage will not be used with this output. It will only\n * become valid for the next connected output.\u003c/p\u003e\n```\n\nIs all we\u0027re committing to in the API, then I don\u0027t think we should do this. However, looking at the current implementation it looks like the new usages should get picked up the next time the producer dequeues a buffer here: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/native/libs/gui/BufferQueueProducer.cpp;drc\u003d045a30e06207744f45d7defa109764a5565bf30e;l\u003d448\n\nSo this only being delayed by the currently in-flight buffers I think is then a reasonable API. We should note that this will trigger re-allocation, could cause producer failures mid-stream if the new usage combination isn\u0027t supported, and thus should be avoided as much as possible regardless.",
      "parentUuid": "16a3d299_da71db47",
      "revId": "af80ce31dfa861b7b912518aeb7523583af84e31",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b1b7e769_69472ffc",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010050
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-18T19:04:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is why I was suggesting making this a system API (apparently, an LL NDK API to be available to codecs), so we don\u0027t commit to somewhat odd stuff in public API. \n\nBut we should document the behavior accurately, of course.  If it\u0027s actually being used for new buffer allocation, it may well crash things; camera service/HAL assume usage won\u0027t change dynamically, so if the buffer layout changes as a result of usage flag changes, there\u0027s definitely a chance things will break when a new buffer is handed off to the HAL to be filled out. But not something we\u0027ve tested at all.",
      "parentUuid": "ee8cee7e_f1668bc4",
      "revId": "af80ce31dfa861b7b912518aeb7523583af84e31",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b6a5dbbd_5af20ccb",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010103
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-18T19:10:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "marking this #llndk instead sounds safer, yeah.\n\nBut as for:\n\n\u003e If it\u0027s actually being used for new buffer allocation, it may well crash things; camera service/HAL assume usage won\u0027t change dynamically, so if the buffer layout changes as a result of usage flag changes, there\u0027s definitely a chance things will break when a new buffer is handed off to the HAL to be filled out.\n\nHopefully camera isn\u0027t currently assuming the set of buffers never changes? Reallocs are already quite possible via public APIs (eg, when passing an Image from an ImageReader to an ImageWriter, since that detaches the buffer from the first queue)\n\nIt\u0027d be unexpected for this to change the format since that\u0027s still set by the producer, so the producer shouldn\u0027t notice this happened other than 1) generic realloc causing cache miss/update, 2) possibly the new usages are incompatible and dequeueBuffer fails entirely which is unusual to happen \u003cN\u003e frames into the stream",
      "parentUuid": "b1b7e769_69472ffc",
      "revId": "af80ce31dfa861b7b912518aeb7523583af84e31",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b7d822b5_041d2d63",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010050
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-18T19:51:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Reallocs should be fine (if very inefficient), though we\u0027ve had some bugs in some camera HALs where bad assumptions have been made (assuming a fixed # of total buffers in terms of mapping buffers to the GPU on a Pixel a few years back, needed for image stabilization warping).\n\nThe main concern would be with IMPLEMENTATION_DEFINED where the actual format might change if the usage flags change.  Most efficient layout for the encoder is often not the same as for the GPU, for example.",
      "parentUuid": "b6a5dbbd_5af20ccb",
      "revId": "af80ce31dfa861b7b912518aeb7523583af84e31",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
